{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779050127,"nonce":"BZ6EU8BWAIvga20Hh1f6I7YIQHc=","title":"Phase 3: deterministic local, SSH, RunPod, and Modal execution contract","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap, Phase 3.\n- Provider contract: `c6c6da0`.\n- Feedbax provider issue: `f68cf66`.\n\n## Problem\nFeedbax needs a deterministic remote/cloud execution contract before Studio grows richer execution UX. Recent RLRMP RunPod work has been effective but agent-improvised: local worktrees are rsynced into `/workspace`, pod readiness logic depends on scattered shell conventions, dependency/path rewrites are fragile, and artifact retrieval is ad hoc. This does not give Feedbax, Mandible, or agents a stable contract for local runs, supplied SSH workers, RunPod pods, or Modal jobs.\n\nWe also want Modal support from the start. Modal may be simpler for parallel independent cells because it provides function-style cloud execution, GPU configuration, autoscaling/map-style parallelism, secrets, images, and volumes. The contract should not bake in RunPod-only assumptions.\n\n## Required direction\nImplement a provider-neutral execution substrate with adapters, not a one-off RunPod script.\n\nFirst-class backends:\n- `local`: run on the current machine for CPU/smoke/dev jobs.\n- `ssh`: run on a user-supplied host with deterministic bootstrap and health checks.\n- `runpod`: allocate or attach to a RunPod pod, then execute through the SSH worker contract.\n- `modal`: submit jobs to Modal using a generated/declared Modal app/function contract, supporting parallel independent cells where practical.\n\n## Contract requirements\n- Versioned execution spec models for job identity, backend, install mode, repo sources, resources, environment, command, artifact policy, and provenance.\n- Explicit install modes: `pypi`, `github-ref`, and `local-rsync`/dev override. Development should prefer GitHub refs when available; local rsync is allowed but must be marked less reproducible and include hashes/provenance.\n- Bootstrap plans must verify code freshness, dependency installation, GPU/JAX health, and lockfile/path sanity before launching a real job.\n- Run scripts must use deterministic log paths, sentinel files, status manifests, and explicit env vars such as `XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false` where appropriate.\n- Artifact sync must distinguish small tracked specs/manifests from bulk outputs such as checkpoints/histories/trajectories/logs.\n- Execution results must emit or point to Feedbax manifests/artifact refs compatible with Mandible ingest.\n- Modal support should account for function/image/volume/secret semantics and parallel submission (`map`/batch-like cells), rather than pretending it is just SSH.\n- RunPod support should account for current practice: single 4090/5090 GPUs, `/workspace`, SSH key config, container/volume sizing, readiness checks, and pod stop/cleanup.\n\n## Initial implementation slice\nBuild the backend-independent schema and orchestration layer plus dry-run/local fixtures first, then wire adapter command generation for SSH/RunPod/Modal sufficiently that the produced plans are inspectable and testable without spending cloud money.\n\nDone means a future Studio/Mandible action can ask Feedbax to validate or prepare an execution for local/SSH/RunPod/Modal, inspect the exact bootstrap/run/artifact/provenance plan, and run a local smoke job that emits a manifest-shaped result. Real cloud submit paths may remain gated/dry-run if credentials are absent, but their specs and generated plans must be concrete enough to implement directly next.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}